<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Third Council of Lima</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1582–1583</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Third Council of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lima">Lima</a> was a church council held in Lima in 1582–1583 under Archbishop Toribio de Mogrovejo. It set the rules of the Catholic Church in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a> for centuries, requiring that indigenous people be taught in their own languages, and commissioned a trilingual catechism in Spanish, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quechua">Quechua</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aymara">Aymara</a>. Printed in Lima in 1584 by Antonio Ricardo, it was the first book printed in South America.</p></div>
